"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/egebeysel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/egebeysel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/egebeysel","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T16:41:28Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"35b2070 (#24749) fixed unbounded stack growth by moving the whole loadProcessorData CPU-feature patch buffer construction to the function entry block. But that also hoisted the feature-bit or/store away from the ukernel call, and once the ukernel inlines, LLVM can no longer store-to-load forward the forced feature bits into the ukernel's runtime feature check across the enclosing loop, so the mmt4d/pack tile-func select never devirtualizes and the microkernel is left out-of-line.\r\n\r\nSplit the two concerns: reserve only the alloca (the stack slot, the actual cause of #24744) in the entry block, but keep the feature-bit patch at the call site. The stores re-run per iteration but allocate no stack, so the stack stays bounded while the forced bits remain adjacent to the (inlined) load and fold as before, restoring devirtualization.\r\n\r\nAssisted-by: Claude-Code","closed_at":"2026-08-13T17:40:22Z","comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/24786/comments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:41:27Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/24786/events","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/pull/24786","id":5073163656,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/24786/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDODGgK6M77Llq7","number":24786,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/pull/24786.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/